[node name="CafeGatheringEncounterStage" instance=ExtResource("1_stage")]
editor_description = "Encounter 9, depth 14,000: the Cheese Cafe. The latest supplied composition drawing is the spatial authority.

LEFT TO RIGHT: the Lantern Keeper is the far-left endpoint; Treasure Hunter and the rat crowd occupy the left-middle; the Miner lands in front-middle; Rotini and the separate dining table sit in the centre-right; and the enlarged cafe is the right-middle anchor. Coco is painted into its serving window, exactly two stools sit under the sill, and Quibble occupies the right stool.

DEPTH IS AUTHORED ACROSS THE SHADER PLANE, NOT ALONG ITS REAR RIM. Screen Y is the depth rule: the cafe, Coco, Quibble, Rotini, and rear rats are highest and furthest back; the dining set, mid rats, and Treasure occupy the middle; the front rats, Keeper, and Miner are lowest and therefore nearest. The Miner's runtime landing settles 56px into that foreground lane. Every overlap agrees with the feet: a lower subject draws or stands in front of a higher subject. The shader supplies a 72px lit shelf and a longer matte transition, so every contact lane remains visibly grounded. CharacterLayer rests at z 4 and the active cutscene at z 5; this stage never goes below local z -1, keeping its furthest background piece at effective z 3 - still strictly above Layer 1 at z 2.

THE CAMERA FOLLOWS THAT SINGLE TABLEAU from RIGHT TO LEFT through typed CAMERA beats. FRAME establishes the cafe at 1.30, then gives Rotini, Coco, Treasure Hunter, the Miner, Quibble, and the Keeper their own smoothly eased close framing. The final 2.4-second move crosses the contiguous cast from the right stool to the far-left Keeper. RESET returns pan and zoom together to gameplay framing. Every move blocks before its speaker talks; CutsceneActionPresenter owns the sine easing, and cancellation or release restores neutral framing.

THE CAFE IS ANOTHER 25 PERCENT LARGER than the previous pass. At 0.16 it is about 249px tall before camera zoom and owns the right-middle like Zephan's paper composition. The room deliberately owes that clearance; cropping the ceiling over the storefront is preferable to shrinking the destination back into a background prop.

THE RAT MASS IS AUTHORED INTO THIS STAGE. Direct cutscene playtest can jump to encounter 9 without activating encounter 8's persistent followers, and those followers track the Miner rather than holding the drawing's place behind Treasure Hunter. Eight bounded, scene-authored actors depict five clumps plus three foreground rats, with no runtime growth.

TRACKING REMAINS ON. The snaking fall arrives across a 49-cell band, so ActorMarkers and PropMarkers slide together from the Miner's actual landing. conversation_root_offset_from_miner_x is the authored Keeper-to-Miner distance (-354px), keeping both camera endpoints stable on every arrival column.

CHEESE GIRL IS DRAWN INTO THE SET. She is painted into the storefront's serving window, so Actors Drawn Into Set names her: the cutscene editor skips her stand-in, and DepthEncounterController places her mark but leaves her presenter hidden. Her line still plays and the box still attributes it to her. Delete the DasQuesoCafe node and she has to come out of that list in the same change, or she disappears from the scene altogether.

Reference: Zephan's supplied paper photo, the later rendered composition, and Decompiled/Handoffs/encounter_9_camera_depth_art_direction.md."
script = ExtResource("15_cafe_stage")
opening_move_seconds = 0.4
closing_move_seconds = 1.2
opening_step_height = 5.0
conversation_pose = &"idle"
hide_actor_after_closing = true
closing_fade_seconds = 1.2
entrance_facing = -1
conversation_facing = -1
closing_facing = -1
conversation_tracks_miner = true
conversation_root_offset_from_miner_x = -354.0
props_track_tracked_cast = true
sequence = ExtResource("12_sequence")
actors_drawn_into_set = Array[StringName]([&"cheese_girl"])

