[node name="rutini" type="Marker2D" parent="ActorMarkers" index="7"]
editor_description = "Immediately left of the cafe, seated behind the left chair at the separate dining table as Zephan dictated. His 20px lane is higher than the 36px table base, so the perspective furniture correctly occludes his lower body without changing his correctly grounded shared appearance."
position = Vector2(-70, 20)

[node name="coffee_cat" type="Marker2D" parent="ActorMarkers" index="8"]
editor_description = "ON THE RIGHT-HAND STOOL, IN FRONT OF THE CAFE WINDOW. Zephan's layout: two stools stand at the serving window Cheese Girl is painted in, and the cat sits on the right one with the coffee he has been carrying since 9,200. The cat and stool share the 12px rear lane; the stool's foreground draw order hides the standing-only art below its seat so Quibble reads as sitting without changing his shared grounding elsewhere."
position = Vector2(235, 12)

[node name="cloak_lantern" type="Marker2D" parent="ActorMarkers" index="9"]
editor_description = "The identity-aware gathering mark for the stage's own visitor. It matches the far-left Conversation mark so the final camera cue resolves the Keeper rather than the fallback spread."
position = Vector2(-530, 58)

[node name="DasQuesoCafe" parent="PropMarkers" index="0" instance=ExtResource("5_cafe")]
editor_description = "THE LARGE RIGHT-MIDDLE ANCHOR from Zephan's paper layout and verbatim direction. The door remains on the building's left and the serving window Coco is painted in remains on its right.

SCALE AND THE ROOM ARE ONE DECISION. 0.16 is another 25 percent increase over the previous 0.12836 pass and makes the 1558px-tall drawing about 249px tall before camera zoom. Its room is re-carved to a 32-cell base clearance in the same change.

Y IS ZERO: the storefront is the rear anchor of the walkable shader plane. The broad rendered shelf now supplies foreground depth instead of asking the building to sink into the cave face.

Z -1, WHICH IS A NUMBER RATHER THAN A TIE. The room now orders strictly: storefront -1, its furniture 0, the cast 1, the foreground set and the front stratum 2.

It sat at 0, the same plane as its own stools, on the assumption that equal z falls back to tree order and index 0 draws first. It does not do so reliably for nodes added to an INHERITED scene, where the index is a hint rather than the child order - and the building drew over its own stools and table, which vanished. Quibble stayed visible only because the cast are a plane in front. Ordering that depends on tree position is ordering that breaks the next time somebody adds a prop. Re-run local_tests/carve_cafe_gathering_room.gd after changing this scale; it refuses to save rather than put the shop's roof in the stone."
z_index = -1
material = SubResource("ShaderMaterial_coco_speaker")
position = Vector2(170, 0)
scale = Vector2(0.16, 0.16)

